A||N||4||chris6878||Tires and rims.....||||3||
Z||000000||chris6878||05-21-2000||01:54 AM||||My fiero currently has stock 14 inch rims on it. I am planning on a set of 15 or 16 inch five stars later..    but i was wondering what results one would get if they downsized the tires on the 14 inch rims. I know this would screw up the speedo a bit..  but wouldn't it lower you cars center of gravity a bit and also have less tire swaying on curves...  probally could actually lower the car an inch, maybe... plus 14 inch tires are cheaper..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>just a thought..||||reg||3
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||05-21-2000||04:19 AM||||Unless you know someone and are able to get tires cheap, I wouldnt bother paying the extra cost for low profile performance 14"ers, You can find a good (cheap) set of stock 15" GT wheels. Most of the time the 15" performance tires are cheaper than the 14"ers because 14 is not a common performance tire size. I just spent over $300.00 on a new set of 14" BFG T/A's <A HREF="http://geocities.com/MotorCity/Pit/5773/002_1a.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://geocities.com/MotorCity/Pit/5773/002_1a.jpg</A>   and I now see so many cheap 15" GT sets for sale. Oh well live and learn. <BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>just my two cents<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 05-21-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000002||phillip||05-21-2000||06:05 AM||||there are enough of the latest cavalier z24 sold to find the wheels fairly cheap. 5 stars that look pretty good and make good "spares" if you still go and get some other 16s later (they are 16 X 6). i got 3 for $75 with 2 good tires. i think some one else mentioned getting a whole set with tires for $200. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||redfiero||05-21-2000||08:18 AM||||I removed my 185/75/14 stock wheels and replaced them with 205/55/16 from a Z24.  I paid $200 for the set with decent tires.  The good thing...the outside diameters of the two are the same...therefore, no change in the speedometer!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shiner||05-21-2000||11:09 AM||||Go with 16"s if you want performance rubber.  Pretty difficult to find much in 15" nowadays.||||reg||1
